@title 3D Heat: the cloud keeps its density from every angle and 100 C+ air is white-hot
@area 3D
# Tadjiro: the cloud changed density when the view went from front to top or side, and very hot spots (100 C+) were hard to tell apart. The cloud now absorbs by millimetre of air on every axis and the same cell size, and air above the top of the cloud scale turns white and more solid. Pictures from several angles are the evidence (painted overlays).
open qa/fixtures/cabinet-cooling-advice.novo
wait 20
click_text 3D #1
wait 30
click_text Heat #1
wait 20
click_text "Settings for the next run"
wait 10
click_text Quick
wait 10
click_text Simulate #2
wait_s 200
expect_not "Preliminary"
click_text Cloud
wait 20
shot cloud-default-view
expect "white-hot"
drag 700 450 700 300
wait 20
shot cloud-from-above
drag 700 300 500 300
wait 20
shot cloud-from-side
drag 500 300 650 380
wait 20
shot cloud-oblique
check_layout
